From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: hub: yield while waiting for the port connect debounce

usb_init() creates one uthread per USB controller for the bus scan
(CONFIG_UTHREAD), but the scan threads never actually overlap: the port
scan loop in usb_device_list_scan() only waits for time to pass
(query_delay, then CONFIG_USB_HUB_DEBOUNCE_TIMEOUT = 1 s for a port with
nothing connected), and for a root hub every port status request is
answered synchronously by the host controller driver, so the loop spins
without ever reaching udelay()/schedule(). The first controller's thread
therefore holds the CPU for the full ~1.1 s debounce, then the next one
does the same, and "usb start" costs ~1.1 s per controller: 7 s on an
H616 board with three EHCI + three OHCI root hubs.

Yield once per pass over usb_scan_list. The other controllers' threads
then configure their root hubs and add their ports to the (shared) list
while the first one is debouncing, and the running loop scans all of
them; the debounce periods overlap and "usb start" takes about one
debounce per phase (primary controllers, then companions). Without
CONFIG_UTHREAD schedule() only runs the cyclic framework, as the EHCI
transfer wait loop already does.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
diff -ruN a/common/usb_hub.c b/common/usb_hub.c
--- a/common/usb_hub.c
+++ b/common/usb_hub.c
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@
 #include <asm/unaligned.h>
 
 #include <usb.h>
+#include <u-boot/schedule.h>
 
 #define USB_BUFSIZ	512
 
@@ -592,6 +593,17 @@
 			if (ret)
 				goto out;
 		}
+
+		/*
+		 * Root hub port status requests complete synchronously, so this
+		 * loop never sleeps while it waits for the connect debounce
+		 * (query_delay + CONFIG_USB_HUB_DEBOUNCE_TIMEOUT) to expire.
+		 * Yield so that the uthreads usb_init() created for the other
+		 * controllers can configure their root hubs and add their ports
+		 * to usb_scan_list meanwhile; the debounce periods then overlap
+		 * instead of adding up per controller.
+		 */
+		schedule();
 	}
 
 out:
